@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — End a tour and show the Podium
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "Child" as child
box "Frontend — game application" #E0F2FE
  participant "SoloGame\n(GameSession)" as solo
  participant "WorldMapPage" as map
  participant "PodiumPage" as page
end box
box "Frontend — components library" #E0F2FE
  participant "PodiumSteps,\nPassportView" as views
end box
box "Frontend — domain library" #E0F2FE
  participant "Tour" as tour
  participant "Standings" as standings
  participant "Passport" as passport
  participant "GameClock" as clock
end box
solo -> tour : applyDuel(winner, now)
solo -> clock : now()
clock --> solo : Time played, pauses left out
solo -> tour : isOver(now)
alt the traveller's distance travelled equals the tour length (L2-006 criteria 1 and 5)
  tour --> solo : Over, all the way round, the traveller wins
else the time limit has passed and the duel has ended (L2-006 criterion 2)
  tour --> solo : Over, time limit, the furthest travelled wins
end
note over solo, tour : When neither has happened the tour is not over and the next duel starts instead.
solo -> tour : result(own player)
tour -> standings : entries()
standings --> tour : Places 1st to last by distance, equal distance\nby who reached it first (L2-006 criteria 3 and 4)
tour -> passport : pages(desks)
passport --> tour : A stamp or a placeholder for each country
tour --> solo : TourResult
solo -> clock : Cancel the duel's timers
solo --> map : TourState phase moving, the last move
map --> child : The last move and its message (L2-030 criterion 4)
map -> solo : continue()
solo --> page : TourState phase over, TourResult (L2-030 criterion 5)
page -> views : Top three, "You went around the world!" or "{name} made it round first!",\nthe winning kid's cheer, passport, count and place (L2-035 criteria 1, 2 and 5)
views --> child : The places rise third, second, first (L2-038 criterion 6)
views --> child : The Podium
@enduml
